

hheellpp                                                         hheellpp



NNAAMMEE
     help - print a brief description of a command's usage

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hheellpp [_c_o_m_m_a_n_d ...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     hheellpp prints a brief description of the usage of each _c_o_m-
     _m_a_n_d. If _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is omitted, hheellpp instead prints a short
     note about itself and then, if the environment variable
     $LLAASSTTEERRRROORR is set, describes the command named there.  If
     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is omitted and $LLAASSTTEERRRROORR is not set, hheellpp exits
     without printing anything further.

     For each _c_o_m_m_a_n_d, hheellpp first looks for the file
     /uussrr/mmaann/ccmmdd/_c_o_m_m_a_n_d or, failing that, /uussrr/mmaann/ccmmdd/_c_o_m-
     _m_a_n_dmm, aanndd, iiff eeiitthheerr eexxiissttss, pprriinnttss tthhee tteexxtt ffoouunndd bbeettwweeeenn
     iittss .HHSS aanndd .HHEE lliinneess.

     Failing that, hheellpp looks for a line #_c_o_m_m_a_n_d in the system
     file /eettcc/hheellppffiillee and, if the environment variable $HHEELLPP
     names a file, in that file as well, and prints the lines
     that follow it up to the next line beginning with #. To
     speed up repeated lookups in a large /eettcc/hheellppffiillee, hheellpp
     maintains an index file, /eettcc/hheellppiinnddeexx, which it rebuilds
     whenever /eettcc/hheellppffiillee is newer than the index.

FFIILLEESS
          /uussrr/mmaann/ccmmdd/_c_o_m_m_a_n_dpreformatted manual page for _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
          /eettcc/hheellppffiillee       system command summaries
          /eettcc/hheellppiinnddeexx      index for /eettcc/hheellppffiillee
          $HHEELLPP               user's own command summaries, if set
          $LLAASSTTEERRRROORR          command described when none is given

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     mmaann

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     hheellpp prints NNoo iinnffoorrmmaattiioonn oonn %ss for any _c_o_m_m_a_n_d it cannot
     find a description for, and exits with a nonzero status if
     any _c_o_m_m_a_n_d could not be described.
